    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Beautifully presented end-of-terrace family home, built  in 2005 to a very high specification and upgraded throughout. This turnkey property offers a converted attic, redesigned kitchen, upgraded bathrooms and a landscaped ESE‑facing rear garden.\r\n\r\nThe interior-designed kitchen features a new layout, new flooring, all new appliances, a gas hob, two electric ovens and an under-counter gas fan heater, while the sitting room enjoys a modern wood-burning stove and bespoke under‑stairs storage. A welcoming entrance seating area, stylish guest WC with frosted glass door, and made‑to‑measure curtains and blinds add to the overall finish.\r\n\r\nThe main bathroom has been fully refitted with new bath, power shower, WC, vanity unit, heated towel rail and three lighting options.\r\n\r\nOutside, a professionally landscaped garden (2019) provides two patio areas, lawn, paving, discreet bin storage and private gate access, backing onto Passage GAA.\r\n\r\nThe house has a BER rate of C1, BER number is 119064210, measures 86.38M2 and has gas central heating and a wood stove providing a warm efficient home. \r\n \r\nThere is ample parking to the front and side and at the far end of the terrace. The property is within easy reach of Douglas ( 14 mins drive), Mahon, Ringaskiddy, Cork Airport and Cork City Centre, and is a short walk from crèche, primary and secondary schools, as well as excellent local walking and cycling routes along the Passage line and nearby coastal paths.\r\nFantastic home, great location and in superb condition."
      },
      {
